ave been  in the form of isakai anime but how  about playing the role of the isekai  protagonist yourself and assembling your  allies rising up the ranks and  conquering a land ravaged by factions  competing for supremacy dying is only  the beginning welcome to the world of  re-fantasia charm and conquer the  sponsors of this video reed fantasia  charm and conquer is the hot new rpg in  town putting you in the role of an  isekai protagonist destined for  greatness but to get to the fight for  supremacy you have to gather your allies  and this my friends is by far my  favorite part of the game you know i'm a  sucker for these waifu collector games  and re-fantasia is no exception the  character art is nothing short of  awesome and it gives me more motivation  to get to know and recruit these  characters who can range from cute to  sexy it's the newest batch in the whole  city builder waifu collector genre so if  you're a fan of this kind of gameplay  you should check this game out it helps  that the game just launched not too long  ago so catching up to the rest of the  player base isn't a problem at all join  the fun by clicking the download link in  the description you can also use the  bonus code for some nifty items that  will come in handy i'm looking forward  to seeing you in game and i hope that we  can have lots of fun memories together  however if you prefer popcorn  entertainment look no further from  misfit of demon king academy in our  number 9 spot  [Music]  foreign  terms of easy access or how easy it is  to get a random guy to watch and enjoy a  show for dumb mindless fun misfit of  demon king academy is my pick not just  for its season but also for its year in  what seems to be one of the last big  hits out of a bygone genre misfit of  demon king academy managed to stand out  and not fall into irrelevance like  around half of the similar stuff flying  around in the early to mid 2010s how so  by taking the overpowered main character  trope and going all overdrive with it  making the thing look so self-aware to  the point of parody while weaving actual  drama and exciting moments in between  them in a way it feels like akashic  records another similar setting that  people cared about amidst the sea of  magic academy shows that we used to get  like five of every season a decade ago  overall it's a show that knows it  doesn't take itself seriously and just  provides a lot of mindless fun coming us  with a lot of power fantasy tropes and  some of the best character and power  designs for the genre it is more than  that however and does come up with some  compelling arcs despite the main  character pretty much being the  spiritual successor of god tsuya  at number eight is a personal favorite  of mine glycemia  i'm not sure how big of a hit death game  survival shows are to you all but  gleibnir has been one of the surprises  of his season i might be a bit biased  because i also like darwin's game and  battle game in five seconds but amongst  those shows i'd say the glyph near was  the one that stood out the most if we're  talking general anime community in  contrast to decadence library took  advantage of all those delays it's just  perception and all but with the big  hitters in its genre mostly out of the  way a lot more people tuned in to glide  play and it wasted no time wowing them  with the pristine fight scenes and very  intriguing story it's just a shame that  this one ended in such a confusing  manner they did an anime original ending  right after starting to tease us with  the big overarching plot because they  probably figured out they wanted an  action finale which wasn't anywhere near  that manga stopping point still the  confusing ending does little to bring  down the enjoyment of the show and i  dare say that the first two-thirds of  gleiphner is legitimately a great show  if you're up for edgy fights a dark  atmosphere and some cool dynamics  between the two contrasting leads  at number seven my pick is glyph near  season mate tower of god  those were the days weren't they back  then there was this movement to bring  korean webtoons in anime former and what  better one to start the movement off  than probably the most popular webtoon  of them all tower of god combining a lot  of the familiar story beats with a very  creative setting and a lot of great  world building and cool characters and  action it's no surprise tower of god  became as famous as it did amongst the  shows i've talked about so far it's  probably the most focused on exploration  and adventure over fights in a sense if  it's the traditional explorative mould  that people have grown to love it's also  got a story that while not as deep or  profound as decadence relatively  speaking it does have its fair share of  substance my only gripe however is that  the entire season is basically the  prologue yeah you've heard that right as  a standalone it does very well and i  really enjoyed it but i think of what it  could have been sure it will get better  soon but i don't see this getting a  second season anytime soon it's a  glorified commercial even more so than  the standard manga or light novel  adaptations and i feel because of that  it's such a waste for number six i'll go  for 86.  [Music]  honestly i haven't had too many chances  to enjoy military anime the past few  years mecca shows i do watch and there  are some great hits from the past  decades like code geass and gundam ibo  there are also fringe military shows as  in barely qualify as one in certain  angles like kimi-san that i enjoyed but  if we're going with something that  speaks more to us in a societal level  coupled with a sci-fi backdrop that's  more of a few decades into the future  instead of a century or millennia it's a  bit harder to find shows like 86. it's a  testament to how unique 86 feels sci-fi  and military aren't rare but the way  it's delivered and how much it acts as  both an exciting action drama a society  study and an ultimately heartwarming  tale of trials and tribulations doesn't  seem as common it's got a little of  everything you'd want from the genre i  dare say that compared to a lot of the  hits that i'll be going over in the  second half it's even more profound and  has themes that speak heavily to the  world at large unfortunately military  and socio-philosophical commentary just  doesn't seem to be as mainstream which  is why it's just a six it's not  underappreciated or anything like that  not at all it's just that given the  package it's in it just finds it hard to  truly break into the mainstream  oh and if you've been enjoying the video  so far good why don't you hit that  little subscribe button and give the  channel a hand i'm happy that a lot of  you guys are enjoying the videos but i'm  finding a large percentage are still not  subscribed so if that's you and you fall  into that category then i would  absolutely love to encourage you to  subscribe like and share the video  my fifth place pick is tokyo revengers  mikey  now here's where the big mainstream hits  start coming in tokyo revenge is by far  has become one of the landmark shows of  2021 combining shonen fair with the time  travel premise that pops up a couple of  times a year yielded what many people  heralded as a unique battle shonen well  unique is probably not something i'll  crown it with completely it does feel  like a change of pace from the  superheroes the demonic powers the fire  breathing the super athletic sword  fights and whatnot it's also more packed  with drama and the gritty atmosphere  you'd expect from a show about  delinquents i give tokyo revenge's  praise mostly for its consistency in  terms of atmosphere it stays consistent  with its tone what it wants to do and  doesn't flip-flop between serious  dramatic moments to comedy that comes  out of nowhere it's a show that derives  its strength from the mature setup for a  battle shonen its attractive premise and  how it manages to hold everything  together in a package all throughout the  run that's probably why it's as popular  as it ended up being  is  here's something that i had mixed  expectations for all we knew about it is  that it was a music oriented action show  with a sci-fi backdrop and that somehow  re-zero guys were behind it dape in  sci-fi and one with terminator light  vibes combined with music truly an  interesting blend of things right it's  easy to look at the special effects and  praise vv is excellent in fields like  music art and awe-inspiring fight scenes  some which i feel holed up damn well a  year after its airing taken down to the  bare bones vivi is a thriller anime that  looks and sounds good and in the fields  it does well it does really well the  amusing thing about vivi however is that  it's one of the shows that i feel  resonate this strongly when it comes to  talking about society's growing infusion  with technology and all the dangers that  come with it it's got some themes that  look more and more relevant the more  years we go through in this world vivi  unlike similar shows like ghost in the  shell may not be remembered in the  slightest years from now heck i feel  it's largely faded from the public  sphere already actually but there's no  doubting its message its core value is a  sci-fi thriller and how fun the ride it  took me through when i first watched it  if we're talking just 2021 it has a case  for being one of the best shows that  that year gave us at third let's look at  ranking of kings  here's a show that's very easy to give a  pass just look at how it looks granted i  fell into the same trap but i eventually  came around to watching it and have to  say that i was blown away for how  simplistic it looks ranking of kings  manages to weave an underdog story for  the ages there's so much that people  give ranking of kings praise for there's  the plot itself there's the music and  presentation and there's a way in which  it creates drama and stakes now i agree  with all of those but for me the  strongest one must be in how it  presented the characters every notable  character no matter how small they are  in the grand scheme of things feels  really fleshed out with their  motivations and character roots ranking  of kings is a classic example of the  famous saying to never judge a book by  its cover its art style unfortunately  holds it back from being blind watched  by people randomly browsing the seasonal  lists looking for something new to watch  but i assure you the journey is worth it  second place is mushoku tensei  how could we talk about the top action  anime of the past few years without  talking about this it's long considered  the pioneer of the whole slew of middle  ages isakai that has oversaturated the  genre so the hype was there there's no  denying what mushoku tensei brings to  the table it's been a while since i've  seen this much love given to adapting a  series where else can you see a studio  being open for the sake of continually  animating a series for years to come it  brings us a visually stunning art a  character who would work for redemption  and strength a thrilling story of  adventure and growth through challenges  and some of the best world building  we've had in isekai for quite some time  it's not without his wrinkles but  putting those aside there's no doubt  that mushoku tensei is one of the most  complete isakai out there it's not  exactly profound or anything like some  of the stuff i've showcased prior but  you can really feel the care given to  its adaptation controversies and all  there's no doubt that mushoku tensei has  a case for being one of the shows the  2020s will be remembered for years to  come for good or bad it depends on your  perspective  for me the top spot belongs to jujutsu  kaizen  it is too early to tell but at the time  of this writing it's clear that jujutsu  kaizen is the battle shonen of the 2020s  i won't call it the best at anything but  in everything things are above average  to great it's got a premise that opens  potential for growth while being easy to  get into it's got a cast that comes in a  whole spectrum of character types the  sound and art is good and it both some  of the best animation we've seen from  new shows the past two years the  excellent production or help elevate the  already interesting magic system when we  do see it come into play creating a lot  of memorable moments and battles a lot  which i've talked about on the channel  you can tell that it kind of feels like  a formula a blueprint for success but  having a blueprint alone isn't enough  see a lot of the one and done battle  shonen but for jiu jitsu kaizen to be  making this kind of legacy for itself is  something the anime team must give  themselves a pat on the back for in the  same vein as wire plays mushoku tensei  ii we just can't ignore its influence in  the number of anime fans it managed to  connect through its popularity it's a  show that i feel partially buoyed off  demon slayer's popularity and brought  back to life the whole genre of  supernatural urban fantasy that was  popular back then with shows like shaman  king and bleach  so how does my list compare to yours  tell me in the comments section what  your top action animate of 2020 to 22r  if you've got more time then don't  forget to check out the channel for  videos that you might enjoy so hit the  subscribe button and don't forget to  check out revantasia the links in the  description once again thanks for  watching i hope that you'll have a great  day ahead and i'm looking forward to  seeing you again thank you  [Music]

